## 3. System Flow Interpretation

The system operates in a **bottom-up analytical flow**:

1. Dependency structures are mapped  
2. Cascading behaviour is simulated  
3. Observability systems attempt detection  
4. Risk signals are classified  
5. Executive layer consolidates system state  

---

## 4. Risk Propagation Pathway

Risk propagation typically follows:
Dependency → Cascade → Observability Gap → Risk Signal Emergence

This represents the key analytical insight of the system:
> failures are not isolated events but propagated structural behaviours

---

## 5. Key Architectural Insight

The architecture highlights a central condition:

> As system coupling increases, observability lag becomes the dominant constraint on system stability.

